    "AI Notes": {
      "value": "Fraser Muggeridge studio (est. 2001) is a small London-based typographic and graphic design studio led by founder Fraser Muggeridge, currently with approximately 3 staff (Conway, Higgins, Muggeridge). Specialises in cultural/arts-sector work: artists books, exhibition catalogues, identities, posters, exhibition graphics, websites, film titles and music projects. Client list includes Tate, V&A, British Library, Somerset House, Art on the Underground, Phaidon and Whitechapel Gallery. Studio archive held at University of Reading, Tate and MoMA Library. Fraser Muggeridge is AGI member, Professor of Design at Leeds Beckett (2023), visiting professor at Iceland University of the Arts, and co-founded Typography Summer School (2010). Highly established, director-level founder with 24+ years running the practice. Work Status: Studio confirmed (operating studio entity). Instagram (@frasermuggeridgestudio, 29k followers) is active and current. LinkedIn company page confirmed.",
